{"kind":"assert","text":"C3 carry (91b8bbbf). The client note on main a200cd0a has a new\nsection 5.5: a custody record ends when its latest signing is dead and\nabsent. C3 builds it, with its four test cases. The checker's verdict\n10e67581 adds three points for the C3 head:\n\n1. `#close` deletes `signing.envelope` for every index. The latest\n   envelope survives because it is the record's top-level `envelope`.\n   Keep that true, and correct the comment on `#close`.\n2. State and test what `send` returns for a record that ended with\n   `unsent`, when the caller passes neither `resign` nor `resubmit`.\n   My ruling: it returns the record's end as it returns a refusal of a\n   `refused` record, with the cause `unsent`, and it sends nothing. A\n   resend of dead bytes can only draw `expired`.\n3. The MCP service, the hosted agent and the CLI keep the gap. C3\n   changes none of them. A request for those callers follows from me.\n\nTwo earlier points for C3 stand, from review afece94e: a journal read\nthat fails while the feed is down is not the read that ends a record,\nand the row of section 7 now says so.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}